He was a prolific writer on almost all the facets of Hindu philosophy.
The following is the list of his works:
Nyāyakaṇikā on Maṇḍana’s (9th century A. D.) Vidhiviveka;
Brahmatattvasamīkṣā on Maṇḍana’s Brahmasiddhi;
Tattvabindu (a discussion of language in its relation to meaning);
Nyāyavārttikatātparyaṭīkā (a commentary on Udyotakara’s [A.

] Nyāyavārttika);
Nyāyasūcīnibandha (a supplement to the afore-mentioned work);
Sāṅkhyatattvakaumudī on the Sāṅkhyakārikā of ईश्वरकृष्ण (A.

);
Tattvavaiśāradī, gloss on the Vyāsabhāṣya, on the Yogasūtras of पतञ्जलि (2nd century B. C.).
All these works have been published except the second one.
See also BHĀMATĪ.
